Found while building the live axum demo (2026-07-31): keeping a guard whose
contract carries a query-semantics invariant produced an artifact the reader
then rejected.

  Error: invalid type: null, expected struct QuerySortContract

Cause: `keep` serializes the whole contract, so an optional field that was
absent when authored is written as an explicit null. The hand written
deserializer in contracts.rs treated a present-but-null key as present and
tried to parse null as the struct.

Consequence: any kept guard carrying that invariant could not load, so the
guard silently stopped guarding. That is a fail-open in the one artifact the
CI gate depends on.

Verified as an affected/fixed pair against the parent file:

  parent (655a95e contracts.rs):
    panicked ... invalid type: null, expected struct QuerySortContract
    test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed
  fixed:
    test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed

The live demo had been working around it by stripping nulls after keep.
